00:25:11,147 --> 00:25:14,230
Speaker 1: That whole thing is electrified to an insane degree.

293
00:25:16,291 --> 00:25:22,715
Speaker 1: But, the other cool thing is that AM radio is amplitude modulation.

294
00:25:23,116 --> 00:25:31,262
Speaker 1: And what that means is that the amplitude of the radio frequency signal is itself the data.

295
00:25:31,762 --> 00:25:41,810
Speaker 1: It gets louder or softer at a ratio to how much strong or weak the RF signal itself is, like it's pulsing almost.

296
00:25:42,671 --> 00:25:56,126
Speaker 1: So if you, say, put a hot dog on the end of a stick, and you ground that hot dog, and you touch that hot dog to an AM antenna, you will hear fucking radio coming out of the hot dog as the hot dog disintegrates.

